1
00:00:00,199 --> 00:00:02,380
Greetings, fellow aliens!

2
00:00:02,380 --> 00:00:07,289
You might wonder why I havn't posted any episode
for a while. The answer is simple : Relativity.

3
00:00:07,289 --> 00:00:13,959
I made a trip with 99.5% light speed. The
trip lasted about one moon cycle for me, but

4
00:00:13,959 --> 00:00:16,360
ten moon cycles for you.

5
00:00:16,360 --> 00:00:23,360
But now I'm back, with a new episode about
a strange and peculiar earthling science : Mathematics.

6
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:59,470
Earthlings' thrive for knowlege is driven
by several factors, like curiosity, doubt,

7
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:02,010
warfare, show-off, and laziness.

8
00:01:02,010 --> 00:01:07,850
The latter, laziness, is what gave rise to
mathematics. We will come back to this later.

9
00:01:07,850 --> 00:01:11,189
In a nutshell, mathematics could be called
"science of truth".

10
00:01:11,189 --> 00:01:15,829
To understand this notion, we have to understand
the earthling concept of true and false.

11
00:01:15,829 --> 00:01:18,310
In other words: Earthling logic.

12
00:01:18,310 --> 00:01:22,020
If you are an alien, you are probably familiar
with the common fuzzy ternary logic:

13
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:26,689
Statements can have the values "True", "false",
"Don't know", or anything in-between.

14
00:01:26,689 --> 00:01:30,090
This is often represented as the "uncertainity
triangle".

15
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:34,149
For those unfamiliar with ternary logic, allow
me to explain.

16
00:01:34,149 --> 00:01:35,420
Imagine a Centauri lottery:

17
00:01:35,420 --> 00:01:40,310
You have a box of six creatures, Tribbles
and Snorks, and you draw one of them, hoping

18
00:01:40,310 --> 00:01:41,469
to get a Tribble.

19
00:01:41,469 --> 00:01:45,009
Now, the claim, "I'll draw a Tribble", will
be true if you know that all the creatures

20
00:01:45,009 --> 00:01:45,899
are Tribbles,

21
00:01:45,899 --> 00:01:49,149
If there are only snorks, the claim will be
false.

22
00:01:49,149 --> 00:01:54,310
If you have three tribbles and three snorks,
the answer is halfway between true and false.

23
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:57,919
If you have no idea what's in the box, the
value is "Don't Know".

24
00:01:57,919 --> 00:02:01,209
When you know that there is one tribble and
two snorks but don't know what the rest is,

25
00:02:01,209 --> 00:02:03,709
the value will be somewhere within the triangle.

26
00:02:03,709 --> 00:02:07,929
Of course, this value depends on what you
know: When you gain information, the value

27
00:02:07,929 --> 00:02:10,149
moves away from the "Don't Know" corner.

28
00:02:10,149 --> 00:02:14,650
That is, in a nutshell, the "uncertainity
triangle".

29
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:19,709
Many alien races only know the three corner
values and don't care about intermediate values.

30
00:02:19,709 --> 00:02:23,709
Political logic is the opposite: The corners
of the triangle are cut of.

31
00:02:23,709 --> 00:02:28,019
An alien politician will never clearly say
something is true, or false, or admit that

32
00:02:28,019 --> 00:02:29,049
he doesn't know.

33
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:34,930
Well, he might say that he didn't know - this
logigal value is called "plausible deniability".

34
00:02:34,930 --> 00:02:37,579
Not everything fits into this schema, though.

35
00:02:37,579 --> 00:02:42,230
The administrative logic used internally by
the Central Galactic Bureaucracy, for instance,

36
00:02:42,230 --> 00:02:43,549
has eleven values:

37
00:02:43,549 --> 00:02:50,549
Approved, Rejected, Wrong-form, Bring-More-Documents,
File-Lost, Not-This-Desk, This-will-take-some-time,

38
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:55,930
Awaiting-Cash, Nothing-I-can-do, Incorrectly-Stamped
and Desk-closed-Come-Back-Later.

39
00:02:55,930 --> 00:03:00,269
The administrative Logic is one of the reasons
nobody really knows how the Bureaucracy works.

40
00:03:00,269 --> 00:03:03,200
Another kind of logic is unary squid logic:

41
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:06,269
The logic of Space squids is based on one
single value, "bloop".

42
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:10,670
The actual information is transmitted in the
nuances on how the "bloop" is pronounced.

43
00:03:10,670 --> 00:03:15,379
It's a bit like the earthling word "awful",
which can mean "very good" or "very bad".

44
00:03:15,379 --> 00:03:17,709
Now, Earthling logic is binary.

45
00:03:17,709 --> 00:03:21,980
Earthling brains are composed of cells called
neurons which have only two states: Silent

46
00:03:21,980 --> 00:03:23,359
and active.

47
00:03:23,359 --> 00:03:28,670
Analougously, earthling logic is based on
two values: False and True. There is no middle ground.

48
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:29,700


49
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:33,099
Earthlings believe that all claims have a
value "true" or "false" - and when you see

50
00:03:33,099 --> 00:03:37,069
neither of them, it's only because the actual
value is hidden.

51
00:03:37,069 --> 00:03:39,780
Earthlings call this imaginary hidden value
"truth".

52
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:43,870
By the way, this binary thinking is the reason
why earthlings have such problems wrapping

53
00:03:43,870 --> 00:03:46,219
their mind around quantum physics.

54
00:03:46,219 --> 00:03:51,390
Their brains can't accept the idea that, for
example, two different realities can coexist

55
00:03:51,390 --> 00:03:52,870
as long as they are not observed.

56
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:57,269
If we combine binary logic with the Earthling
concept of "things", we get set theory.

57
00:03:57,269 --> 00:04:02,299
A set is a collection of elements, mathematical
entities that stand for any kind of "things".

58
00:04:02,299 --> 00:04:07,219
Elements are either in a set or outside: Earthling
logic knows no middle ground.

59
00:04:07,219 --> 00:04:11,379
The earthling logic leads what earthling call
"conclusions": Rules for combining claims

60
00:04:11,379 --> 00:04:13,579
to get new claims.

61
00:04:13,579 --> 00:04:17,940
Conclusions are what the fabric of mathematics
is made of - we will come back to that point.

62
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:18,190
But mathematics is not only about abstract
conclusions.

63
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,209
It has another, much more practical aspect:
Mathematics is a way to avoid calculating.

64
00:04:19,209 --> 00:04:23,210
What's calculating? Well, calculating is a
way to avoid counting, or more generally measuring.

65
00:04:23,210 --> 00:04:25,060
Let me elaborate.

66
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:28,730
Every young planetary civilization has to
find a way to measure resources:

67
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:34,420
Population, arable land, food, real estate,
raw materials, time : 

68
00:04:34,420 --> 00:04:35,770
All this needs to be properly measured.

69
00:04:35,770 --> 00:04:42,220
Also, construction requires measuring quantities
like lengths, areas, volumes and angles beforehand.

70
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:46,450
Small quantities can be measured directly,
but things get more complicated when the quantities

71
00:04:46,450 --> 00:04:48,870
are either bigger or not easy to measure.

72
00:04:48,870 --> 00:04:53,370
That's when calculating comes in: It's a shortcut,
a way to combine available quantities to get

73
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:54,760
other quantities.

74
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:58,250
In other ways, calculating equals measuring
times laziness.

75
00:04:58,250 --> 00:05:00,760
Every alien race has its own calculating methods.

76
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:06,770
The Aldebaranians, for example, use a curve,
to multiply values. It's a strange method,

77
00:05:06,770 --> 00:05:07,820
but it works.

78
00:05:07,820 --> 00:05:12,640
Now, the bigger a civilization becomes, the
more things are to calculate.

79
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:16,780
That's usually the point when a planet's bio-administrator
gives the civilization limited access to the

80
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:20,890
Great Galactic Grid, and thus to planetary
superbrains which do the calculation work

81
00:05:20,890 --> 00:05:22,210
for the whole galaxy.

82
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:27,030
The access to superbrains is completely free
- at least for some hundred solar cycles.

83
00:05:27,030 --> 00:05:31,790
But once the civilization is completely dependent
on external computer power, a Tax Star portals

84
00:05:31,790 --> 00:05:36,450
into orbit and the planet becomes full tax-paying
member of the Galactic Bureaucracy.

85
00:05:36,450 --> 00:05:39,010
At this point, they don't have much of a choice.

86
00:05:39,010 --> 00:05:42,660
The "computation monopoly" of the Planetary
Superbrains make them one of the powers that

87
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:47,670
run the Central Galactic Bureaucracy, alongside
with the Tax Authority, the Control Bureau,

88
00:05:47,670 --> 00:05:52,830
the Apparatus, the Galactic Intelligence,
the Space Force, the Comitee, the Galactic

89
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:53,710
Bank...

90
00:05:53,710 --> 00:05:55,500
Well, it's complicated.

91
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:59,700
Actually, nobody really knows who pulls the
strings in the Galaxy.

92
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:04,450
But Mankind had no bio-admin and no access
to superbrains - so they had to develop their

93
00:06:04,450 --> 00:06:07,910
own way to deal with computations: Mathematics.

94
00:06:07,910 --> 00:06:12,170
Basically, mathematics is a way of avoiding
calculating , and calculating is a way of

95
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:14,300
avoiding measuring and counting.

96
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:18,600
That's why we could define "Mathematics equals
measuring times laziness squared".

97
00:06:18,600 --> 00:06:20,850
Tips for tourists:

98
00:06:20,850 --> 00:06:25,570
In general, Earthling books are an interesting
and exotic souvenir.

99
00:06:25,570 --> 00:06:30,420
However, mathematics is considered contraband
by Galactic laws, because it threatens the computation

100
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:32,520
monopoly of the Superbrains.

101
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:36,430
You don't want to run into a hyperspace patrol
with a math book on board - it could get you

102
00:06:36,430 --> 00:06:38,560
into serious trouble.

103
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:42,340
The first contact of aliens with mathematics
goes back many millennia.

104
00:06:42,340 --> 00:06:46,630
More than four thousand solar cycles ago,
a couple of alien information smugglers landed

105
00:06:46,630 --> 00:06:50,350
In a region called Egypt, and offered the
earthlings advanced computation methods and

106
00:06:50,350 --> 00:06:54,130
the exact value of Pi, in exchange for the
recipe for beer.

107
00:06:54,130 --> 00:06:59,400
The Egyptians politely declined: Their computation
methods were sufficient to build huge pyramids,

108
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:02,870
not to speak of the logistics required to
pay and house thousands of workers and to

109
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:05,870
move millions of tons of calcium carbonate.

110
00:07:05,870 --> 00:07:10,430
As for Pi, they had already incorporated Pi
into the dimensions of some of their pyramids,

111
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:13,120
using rolled and stacked cylindrical barrels.

112
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:17,380
To construct their pyramids, the Egyptians
had developed something called Geometry:

113
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:19,000
The theory of shapes.

114
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:24,620
In a nutshell, geometry is all about lines,
angles, and areas, and how to avoid measuring

115
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:25,500
them.

116
00:07:25,500 --> 00:07:29,870
The information smugglers came back a thousand
solar cycles later, this time in Babylonia.

117
00:07:29,870 --> 00:07:34,970
But the Babylonians were not impressed. Their
mathematicians knew the Pythagorean theorem,

118
00:07:34,970 --> 00:07:39,020
could solve quadratic equations and were able
to compute the square root of two, with an

119
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:41,340
error of one ten-thousandth.

120
00:07:41,340 --> 00:07:45,660
More generally, the Babylonians had developped
the art of manipulating numbers. Earthlings

121
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:47,550
call this Arithmetics.

122
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:48,140
What are numbers ?

123
00:07:48,140 --> 00:07:53,890
Well, it has to do with "things". To quantify
things, earthlings invented numbers, a series

124
00:07:53,890 --> 00:07:58,550
of abstract "things", called 1 2 3 4 5 6 7
etc. .

125
00:07:58,550 --> 00:08:02,990
Think of numbers as a series of imaginary
stickers. Whenever earthlings want to quantify

126
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:08,270
things, they glue the stickers onto them,
one by one. This is called "counting".

127
00:08:08,270 --> 00:08:12,360
The last assigned sticker indicates the quantity
of things, their "number".

128
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:16,970
Earthlings are obsessed with numbers. They
count and number everything: Houses, offspring,

129
00:08:16,970 --> 00:08:21,530
vehicles, books, even kings, and gods - everything.

130
00:08:21,530 --> 00:08:26,430
Except for the microbes.

131
00:08:26,430 --> 00:08:31,600
There are many ways to represent numbers.
But the most common way is the decimal system.

132
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:36,030
Numbers are written as series of digits - nine
of them correspond to the numbers 1 to 9,

133
00:08:36,030 --> 00:08:38,110
and an "empty" digit called zero.

134
00:08:38,110 --> 00:08:42,270
The ten digits come from the fact that earthlings
have ten fingers - the bony tentacles at the

135
00:08:42,270 --> 00:08:44,420
end of their upper extremities.

136
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:49,010
Some ancient civilizations used a base-12
system or a base-60 system, which are more

137
00:08:49,010 --> 00:08:53,930
useful for divisions. You'll still find remains
of both systems, in particular for measuring

138
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,470
time.

139
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:59,720
Earthling computers use a base-2 system, as
they are based on true-false logic, not on

140
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:03,190
true-false-don't-know logic like most alien
computers.

141
00:09:03,190 --> 00:09:08,110
By the way, Squids have a similar system - but
it's a base-one-system which contains only

142
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:11,990
the digit zero. Any number above zero can't
be expressed in this system and is called

143
00:09:11,990 --> 00:09:12,840
"some".

144
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:17,100
The earthlings found numbers quite useful
- and whe earthlings find something useful,

145
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:21,330
you can bet that they want more of it. For
starters, they took the digit 0 and made it

146
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:24,160
a number, closing the gap below the 1.

147
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:28,960
Generally, earthling mathematicians don't
like gaps. For example, when you substract

148
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:34,980
5 from 2, you fall into a gap "below zero".
So, earthlings invented negative numbers.

149
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:40,500
Likewise, when you divide 5 by 2, you fall
into the gap between 2 and 3. so the earthlings

150
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:45,500
invented fractions, aka rational numbers.
Those numbers can be represented as a nice

151
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:46,900
straight line.

152
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:51,740
In ancient Egypt and Babylon, mathematics
was just a set of practical rules, a toolbox

153
00:09:51,740 --> 00:09:56,380
for architects and bookkeepers. But this approach
was about to change.

154
00:09:56,380 --> 00:10:02,940
About 2300 solar cycles ago, our alien information
smugglers came back a third time, again in

155
00:10:02,940 --> 00:10:03,410
Egypt.

156
00:10:03,410 --> 00:10:06,920
Here they met a greek mathematician named
Euclid who had developped a wholly new approach

157
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,700
to mathematics: Axioms.

158
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:14,420
Realizing they had nothing to top that, our
aliens left, never to return again.

159
00:10:14,420 --> 00:10:20,070
But what are those axioms? Well, axioms are
fundamental assumptions you build a theory

160
00:10:20,070 --> 00:10:26,060
upon. Take, for example, the natural numbers
1 2 3 4 5 etc. .

161
00:10:26,060 --> 00:10:29,510
Those numbers can be described with the so-called
Peano axioms:

162
00:10:29,510 --> 00:10:31,459
- There is a number called zero.

163
00:10:31,459 --> 00:10:33,280
- Every number has a successor.

164
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,130
- Zero is successor of nobody.

165
00:10:35,130 --> 00:10:37,319
- No two numbers have the same successor.

166
00:10:37,319 --> 00:10:41,810
- If a property holds for 0, and it propagates
from each number to its successor, then it

167
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:44,750
holds for all numbers. This is called "induction".

168
00:10:44,750 --> 00:10:50,500
Given any set of axioms, you can use logic
to construct a whole building of conclusions.

169
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:54,930
Interesting conclusions are called "theorems".
That's basically how the whole of modern mathematics

170
00:10:54,930 --> 00:10:56,540
is built.

171
00:10:56,540 --> 00:11:00,920
Note that mathematicians don't think axioms
are based on "truth". They are just assumptions

172
00:11:00,920 --> 00:11:06,250
to start with. Mathematicians like to play
with axioms, omit this one or add that one,

173
00:11:06,250 --> 00:11:07,980
and see what happens.

174
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:11,970
Note that mathematics never says "That is
true", but rather "Given this and this, you

175
00:11:11,970 --> 00:11:16,940
can conclude that". In other words, mathematical
theorems are always true, because they are

176
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:18,940
elaborate tautologies.

177
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:22,460
One could define mathematics as "hunt for
interesting tautologies".

178
00:11:22,460 --> 00:11:26,860
This is the theoretical side of mathematics
- there is still the practical one:

179
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:29,000
Measuring times lazyness squared.

180
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,170
Now, according to mathematicians, doing mathematics
is not so much constructing into the sky as

181
00:11:34,170 --> 00:11:36,860
it is exploring an unknown territory.

182
00:11:36,860 --> 00:11:40,810
You have to construct the roads and bridges,
but the landscape is already there, waiting.

183
00:11:40,810 --> 00:11:44,130
So, let's explore a bit the landscape of mathematics,
shall we?

184
00:11:44,130 --> 00:11:49,750
At the very center we have basic logic, and
the two disciplines Geometry and Arithmetics.

185
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:54,380
As said before, Geometry is all about shapes
and measures, and arithmetics is all about

186
00:11:54,380 --> 00:11:56,180
numbers and operations.

187
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:59,880
This is the starting point for the exploration
of mathematics.

188
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:03,430
Starting from here, we will discover several
regions of mathematics:

189
00:12:03,430 --> 00:12:06,260
Number theory and algebra, which are derived
from arithmetics,

190
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:08,710
Topology, which comes from geometry,

191
00:12:08,710 --> 00:12:12,570
and Analysis, which is arithmetics used to
measure geometry.

192
00:12:12,570 --> 00:12:18,040
Let's start with topology. Topology is, so
to speak, geometry minus measuring.

193
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:21,779
It's kind of "rubber geometry", it considers
properties of shapes that don't change when

194
00:12:21,779 --> 00:12:23,279
you deform them.

195
00:12:23,279 --> 00:12:27,790
If you explore the properties of natural numbers,
you get to number theory. Number theorists

196
00:12:27,790 --> 00:12:32,860
are particularly fond of prime numbers - numbers
that can't be broken down into smaller factors.

197
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:37,350
Now, arithmetics can be further generalized,
with a little trick mathematicians are fond

198
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:38,060
of.

199
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:44,690
First, you take an example - say, the natural
numbers. Secondly, you state some basic rules.

200
00:12:44,690 --> 00:12:49,270
And third, you forget about the example and
consider those rules as axioms.

201
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:52,880
This is exactly how arithmetics is generalized
into Algebra.

202
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:57,060
For example, "Adding", can not only be applied
to numbers, but also to other things like

203
00:12:57,060 --> 00:13:03,270
arrows, spatial movements, permutations, rotations,
or even dancing steps.

204
00:13:03,270 --> 00:13:07,930
Roughly speaking: When you generalize the
rules for addition , you get semi-groups.

205
00:13:07,930 --> 00:13:13,250
When you include subtraction, you get groups.
When you allow multiplication, you get rings.

206
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:16,880
And when you make sure you can divide, you
get fields.

207
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:20,940
This belongs all to the domain of Algebra.
In a certain manner, algebra is all about

208
00:13:20,940 --> 00:13:24,650
manipulating symbols.

209
00:13:24,650 --> 00:13:24,970
Scientific advice.

210
00:13:24,970 --> 00:13:29,490
If you are a Xeno-biologist, you probably
know Bloblings - jellyfish-like creatures

211
00:13:29,490 --> 00:13:31,620
of various shapes. Now, the classification
of bloblings is basically a problem of topology

212
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:38,620
- but you can do it using group theory. In
other words, adding and subtracting.

213
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:44,960
See, bloblings are into what earthlings would
call bondage - they like to wrap closed rubber

214
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:46,450
bands around their body.

215
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:52,649
There are countless bondage methods, but you
can define "addition" and "subtraction" between

216
00:13:52,649 --> 00:13:53,600
bondage loops:

217
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:55,830
This loop plus that loop is that loop, or
that loop minus twice this loop is that loop.

218
00:13:55,830 --> 00:14:01,529
Now, for this particular blobling, all bondage
variantes can be obtained by combining two

219
00:14:01,529 --> 00:14:04,800
loops : Through the hole, and around the hole.

220
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:06,710
Mathematicians would say it is a group of
rank two.

221
00:14:06,710 --> 00:14:11,839
Other bloblings need four loops, or six, or
fourteen. This number doesn't change when

222
00:14:11,839 --> 00:14:15,310
we deform the blobling - that's something
topologists really like.

223
00:14:15,310 --> 00:14:19,870
So, this number can be used to classify the
bloblings.

224
00:14:19,870 --> 00:14:24,130
If this was a bit too much for you, don't
mind - the important thing here is that we

225
00:14:24,130 --> 00:14:27,050
can use algebra to solve problems in topology.

226
00:14:27,050 --> 00:14:32,160
This domain halfway between topology and algebra
is called algebraic TOPOLOGY.

227
00:14:32,160 --> 00:14:36,029
Algebra is a bit like what earthlings call
magic: You manipulate some symbols and apply

228
00:14:36,029 --> 00:14:41,290
some formulae - and suddenly you have performed
something completely unrelated.

229
00:14:41,290 --> 00:14:45,770
One could say that any sufficiently evolved
algebra is indistinguishable from magic.

230
00:14:45,770 --> 00:14:50,089
This holds even more for another discipline:
Category theory. This theory is all about

231
00:14:50,089 --> 00:14:51,500
stuff connected with arrows.

232
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:56,460
It looks like fiddle-faddle but is surprisingly
useful. Mathematicians call the use of category

233
00:14:56,460 --> 00:14:59,220
theory in other disciplines "abstract nonsense".

234
00:14:59,220 --> 00:15:03,350
I'm not joking, it's called like that. "Abstract
nonsense".

235
00:15:03,350 --> 00:15:09,240
Now, we have seen two big regions of mathematics:
Topology, which is basically geometry minus

236
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:12,860
measuring, and algebra, which is arithmetics
minus numbers.

237
00:15:12,860 --> 00:15:16,720
A third big field of mathematics takes the
numbers from arithmetics and uses them to

238
00:15:16,720 --> 00:15:19,750
measure geometry. This is called Analysis.

239
00:15:19,750 --> 00:15:24,810
To understand analysis, we first have to understand
something else: Infinity.

240
00:15:24,810 --> 00:15:29,370
What's infinity? Well, it's another gap-filler:
When you count and count onwards, the numbers

241
00:15:29,370 --> 00:15:35,690
actually go nowhere. So mathematicians invented
a number "behind" all natural numbers: Infinity.

242
00:15:35,690 --> 00:15:40,000
Once you have the concept of infinity, you
can observe, for example, infinitely long

243
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,160
increasing sequences of numbers.

244
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:47,410
Some tend to infinity, others approach some
rational number - but there are others that

245
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:49,860
approach nothing, that fall into a gap.

246
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:54,050
But mathematicians don't like gaps. So they
defined a new kind of numbers to fill the

247
00:15:54,050 --> 00:15:55,730
gaps: Real numbers.

248
00:15:55,730 --> 00:15:59,860
A real number is anything that can be approached
by an infinite sequence of numbers.

249
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:06,020
Now, real numbers are very useful to measure
things - lengths, angles, areas, time and

250
00:16:06,020 --> 00:16:11,209
so on. Analysis is particularly interested
in "functions" - measures that change over

251
00:16:11,209 --> 00:16:11,959
time.

252
00:16:11,959 --> 00:16:18,010
This leads to two things: Accumulated values,
or "integrals", and change rates, or "differentials".

253
00:16:18,010 --> 00:16:22,440
Turns out that the one is actually the inverse
of the other. That's the Fundamental Theorem

254
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,089
of Calculus.

255
00:16:24,089 --> 00:16:28,370
Analysis has many practical applications in
engineering and natural science, particularly

256
00:16:28,370 --> 00:16:34,600
physics. We will speak about earthling sciences
in another episode.

257
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:36,230
Strategic advice:

258
00:16:36,230 --> 00:16:40,040
When attacking a planet, a common tactic is
to cut off the defender from the Great Galactic

259
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:45,290
Grid, to block all ballistic computations.
However, earthlings' artillery doesn't need

260
00:16:45,290 --> 00:16:50,610
to access the Grid, they use mathematics.
So you better anticipate precisely aimed artillery

261
00:16:50,610 --> 00:16:53,440
fire.

262
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:58,450
With real numbers, mathematicians have filled
most of the gaps. But one gap remains:

263
00:16:58,450 --> 00:17:02,930
There is still no square root of minus one,
or any other negative number. So mathematicians

264
00:17:02,930 --> 00:17:06,110
invented a square root of minus one and called
it "i".

265
00:17:06,110 --> 00:17:09,699
They didn't quite know where to put it, so
they put it it above the line.

266
00:17:09,699 --> 00:17:14,149
This new number, and everything you can create
by combining real numbers with i, are the

267
00:17:14,149 --> 00:17:15,309
complex numbers.

268
00:17:15,309 --> 00:17:20,249
Back to our mathematical landscape. Like between
algebra and topology, there are interdisciplinary

269
00:17:20,249 --> 00:17:22,839
fields between analysis and the other fields.

270
00:17:22,839 --> 00:17:26,769
When you combine analysis with topology, you
get differential geometry - the theory of

271
00:17:26,769 --> 00:17:29,549
shapes with notions of length and angles.

272
00:17:29,549 --> 00:17:33,879
It's very useful, for example for speculating
about the shape of the universe.

273
00:17:33,879 --> 00:17:37,820
On the border between analysis and algebra
we have algebraic geometry - the theory of

274
00:17:37,820 --> 00:17:43,159
shapes defined by polynomials. One example
would be this heart-shaped surface, which

275
00:17:43,159 --> 00:17:45,549
is defined by this equation.

276
00:17:45,549 --> 00:17:49,629
Earthling viewers, feel free to forward the
formula to mathematically inclined reproduction

277
00:17:49,629 --> 00:17:53,129
partners. I understand earthlings like to
do such things.

278
00:17:53,129 --> 00:17:57,320
I don't know why. It's probably a ritual.

279
00:17:57,320 --> 00:18:01,259
There are many other mathematical disciplines,
for example probability theory.

280
00:18:01,259 --> 00:18:05,619
It's basically an extension of binary logic
to the whole true-false-edge of the uncertainity

281
00:18:05,619 --> 00:18:07,100
triangle.

282
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:10,899
Earthlings think that even uncertain claims
are somewhere between true and false.

283
00:18:10,899 --> 00:18:14,019
There is still a whole dimension missing,
but it's already an improvement.

284
00:18:14,019 --> 00:18:18,379
I will conclude with a theorem that doesn't
belong to the fields mentioned above.

285
00:18:18,379 --> 00:18:22,450
It's rather out in the ocean of Logic and
meta-mathematics. I'm speaking of G�del's

286
00:18:22,450 --> 00:18:23,739
first theorem.

287
00:18:23,739 --> 00:18:27,220
It's closely related to Earthlings' "true
or false" logic.

288
00:18:27,220 --> 00:18:32,529
See, most mathematical claims in a theory
can either be proven true, or proven false.

289
00:18:32,529 --> 00:18:35,730
But G�del constructed a claim that says
"I can't be proven".

290
00:18:35,730 --> 00:18:39,820
The claim can't be false - otherwise it would
be a false provable claim; and that would

291
00:18:39,820 --> 00:18:40,899
be nonsense.

292
00:18:40,899 --> 00:18:44,580
So, according to earthling logic, it must
be true.

293
00:18:44,580 --> 00:18:48,989
But if it's true, it is right about being
unprovable. So we have a claim that is true,

294
00:18:48,989 --> 00:18:51,090
but you can't prove it within the theory.

295
00:18:51,090 --> 00:18:55,590
In other words, mathematics can prove a lot,
but it will never be able to prove or disprove

296
00:18:55,590 --> 00:18:58,519
everything, there will always be open questions.

297
00:18:58,519 --> 00:19:01,409
This was the thirteenth' episode of Earthlings
101.

298
00:19:01,409 --> 00:19:06,279
The next episode will be about the two thinking
systems Earthlings have : Intuition and reason.

299
00:19:06,279 --> 00:19:10,249
But before that, I'll have to make the third
and last episode of my "No Edge" series about

300
00:19:10,249 --> 00:19:11,919
the shape of the universe.

301
00:19:11,919 --> 00:19:13,799
Subscribe if you don't want to miss it.

302
00:19:13,799 --> 00:19:20,799
Thanks for watching, and as always: Don't
